diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..6f825ea 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,8 +2,40 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Event delivery
+
+When a subscribed event is committed, each active webhook on that board gets a
+JSON `POST` to its payload URL. Events that roll back are not delivered. The
+payload contains the event's `id`, `action`, `created_at`, `creator`, `board`,
+`eventable`, `card`, and action-specific `particulars`. URLs include the account
+slug. Slack, Campfire, and Basecamp chat URLs receive their native message shapes
+(`text`, `body`, and `content`, respectively).
+
+Requests include:
+
+- `X-Webhook-Id`: the stable delivery ID, which receivers can use to deduplicate.
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: the event's creation time in UTC.
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the exact request body,
+  using the webhook's signing secret.
+
+There is one send attempt per event/receiver pair. Duplicate jobs cannot send it
+again, and failed or timed-out POSTs are not retried. Exactly-once receipt cannot
+be guaranteed over HTTP: a receiver may process a request whose response never
+reaches the sender. Receivers should deduplicate by `X-Webhook-Id` when needed.
+Only public destinations are contacted; redirects are not followed.
+
+Any 2xx response is a success. HTTP status codes and transport errors are recorded
+in delivery history. A receiver is deactivated after at least ten consecutive
+failures **and** at least one hour since the first failure in that streak. A
+successful delivery resets the streak, as does manual reactivation. Deliveries
+already queued for an inactive receiver are not sent.
+
+Delivery history is kept for seven days, with older entries removed by the
+recurring cleanup task every fifteen minutes. Failure streaks survive log cleanup.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
+
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
 
 __Response:__
diff --git a/test/jobs/webhook/delivery_job_test.rb b/test/jobs/webhook/delivery_job_test.rb
